    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it can.  A \"switch the target of attack\" effect such as ＜Raid＞ affects the attacking Digimon itself, therefore the target of attack can be switched to a Digimon that isn't affected by effects.",
        "question": "When \"isn't affected by your opponent's effects\" is gained from this card's [When Digivolving] effect, can the target of attack be switched to this Digimon using a \"switch the target of attack\" effect such as ＜Raid＞ on an opponent's Digimon?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it activates.",
        "question": "Does this card’s [All Turns] effect activate when a security card is removed from my security stack by one of my own effects?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it activates.",
        "question": "Does the \"then\" part of this card's [When Digivolving] effect activate even if [Magnamon (X Antibody)] or an [Armor Form] trait card isn't in this Digimon's digivolution cards?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
